{"content":[{"c":["BERACAH*, V",{"c":["alley of"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"}],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Place where King Jehoshaphat gathered the people of Judah to praise the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.26","r":"2Chr.20.26","rawR":"2Chr.20.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.26","value":"2Chr.20.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 20:26"},"). The people were grateful for God’s help in defeating the attacking armies of Moab, Ammon, and Mt Seir (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.1-25","r":"2Chr.20.1-25","rawR":"2Chr.20.1-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.1-25","value":"2Chr.20.1-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 20:1-25"},"). It is most often identified with the area Wadi el ’Arrub, not far from Tekoa, where a ruin called Bereikut exists."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BeracahValleyof","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Chr 20:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.20.26","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.20.26","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.20.26"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 20:1-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.20.1-25","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.20.1-25","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.20.1-25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"43a6de0e8bb6a955d13609ecfb53bb991dc4d28cd0eb79b35c655730f6e7f16c","sourceItemName":"BeracahValleyof","sourceItemOrder":199,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BeracahValleyof","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beracah*, Valley of","title":"Beracah*, Valley of","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}